  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feed the Future Zimbabwe Non-timber Forest Products (NTFP) GDA Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zimbabwe):  The Non-Timber Forest Products (NTFP) activity is based on a Global Development Alliance (GDA) between USAID and a local private sector partner, Organic Africa Holdings. This activity aims to improve the resilience of vulnerable and marginalized communities, particularly women and youth,through increased household incomes and strengthened environmental stewardship from the commercialization of NTFPs in seven provinces. The activity will increase the supply of NTFPs that meet market requirements through targeted training of 12,000 community-based collectors and smallholder farmers; investments in primary processing equipment for raw materials; and alignment with local regulations and international certification standards of NTFPs, including organic, FairWild, Fairtrade, and Kosher. In addition, the activity will support communities to sustainably use and protect forest areas. Most beneficiaries in these regions are women. Increasing women&apos;s financial contributions to their households will improve their status in their communities and will contribute to reducing gender-based violence.</narrative>
  </description>
